  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The range of a tower in the communication system is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>Range</mtext><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>h</mi><mi>R</mi></msqrt></math></p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Height of the tower,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;radius of Earth</p><p>Given, The range of tower is to be doubled.</p><p>As, Range&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8733;</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, to make the range double, the height&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi></math>&nbsp;have to be made&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;times.</p></blockquote>"
